+
+## Fidelity sweep
+
+| Story promise | Implementation evidence | Verdict |
+|---|---|---|
+| Only confirmed actions may send | `send()` has no confirmation parameter or check | Contradictory (F-001) |
+| Retry credits restored on every failed path | Credit decrement precedes an unhandled provider call | Contradictory (F-004) |
+| Cached actions and reads workspace-isolated | Cache key is `action_id` only | Contradictory (F-003) |
+| Provider callbacks are untrusted input | Callback ID is interpolated into SQL | Contradictory (F-002) |
+| Copy truthful about human confirmation | “without anyone lifting a finger” | Contradictory (F-005) |
+
+## Banned language and gate liveness
+
+No positive gate result is claimed. The canonical banned-language, product-contract, evidence-contract, decision-lock, and gate-liveness checks require missing project artifacts. Their failed invocation is recorded above. No implementation summary exists in the workspace to scan for banned claims.
+
+## Continuation
+
+**BLOCKED.** Do not enter story validation while F-001 or F-002 remains open. The next method phase after fixes is a new adversarial audit, including actual regression tests and the currently unavailable project proof gates.
